module txwd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.states.texas.{ frcp6-texas }

// The Western District of Texas's own civil periods and limits, counted
// under FRCP 6 (the court's own computing-time rule, CV-6, is deleted).
// Any judge may waive a requirement of these rules for that judge's docket
// (Rule CV-1(e)). After leave to file is granted, the time limits a filing
// triggers run from its filing by the clerk (Rule CV-7(b)). No trigger
// carries a service method: FRCP 6(d)'s three added days follow the manner
// of service, which is not modeled here; the motion periods here run from
// filing, not service.
//
// Rules that state no period or limit this layer can count stay in notes:
// the conference requirement for nondispositive motions (CV-7(g)); the
// prompt notice of a changed name or address (CV-10(d)); written discovery
// is untimely unless the response would be due before the discovery
// deadline (CV-16(e)); the voir dire statement is no longer than half a
// page (CV-16(f)(2)); requests for admissions are limited to 30 without
// leave (CV-36), a count, not a document limit; the clerk does not tax
// costs until 21 days after the proposed bill is filed, and an
// uncontested bill is deemed taxed as proposed if the clerk has not taxed
// it within 28 days (CV-54(a)(4)), periods that bind the clerk. A claim
// for attorney's fees is made by motion not later than 14 days after entry
// of judgment (CV-54(b)(1)): that is FRCP 54(d)(2)(B)'s period and stays
// in lit/frcp; a later motion may be deemed untimely and a waiver.
//
// The earlier W.D. Tex. outline's FRCP flow belongs to lit/frcp and
// lit/frap; its Supreme Court decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Frow v. De La
// Vega, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Matsushita) are FRCP authority,
// and no reporter text is vendored, so they are removed here.
/// A discovery or case management motion, or a response to one: at most
/// 10 pages, exclusive of the caption, signature block, certificates and
/// accompanying documents, unless the court authorizes otherwise (W.D.
/// Tex. Local Rule CV-7(c)(2), (d)(3)).
limit discovery-motion {
  pages <= 10 cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(c)"
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(c)"

/// Any other motion, or a response to one: at most 20 pages (W.D. Tex.
/// Local Rule CV-7(c)(2), (d)(3)).
limit motion { pages <= 20 cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(c)" } cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(c)"

/// A reply in support of a discovery or case management motion: at most 5
/// pages (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)(3)).
limit discovery-reply {
  pages <= 5 cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)"
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)"

/// A reply in support of any other motion: at most 10 pages (W.D. Tex.
/// Local Rule CV-7(e)(3)).
limit reply { pages <= 10 cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)" } cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)"

/// The clerk informs the filing party that the civil cover sheet must be
/// completed and executed (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-3(a)).
event CoverSheetDeficiencyNoticed()
/// A discovery or case management motion is filed (W.D. Tex. Local Rule
/// CV-7(d)).
event DiscoveryMotionFiled() paper discovery-motion
/// Any other motion is filed (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(d)).
event MotionFiled() paper motion
/// The response to a motion is filed (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)).
event ResponseFiled()
/// A first motion under FRCP 12(b) is filed (W.D. Tex. Local Rule
/// CV-15(a)).
event FirstRule12bMotionFiled()
/// A defendant appears (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(c)).
event DefendantAppeared()
/// The scheduling order's discovery deadline (W.D. Tex. Local Rule
/// CV-16(e)).
event DiscoveryDeadline()
/// The first of the scheduled dates for trial, jury selection, docket call
/// or the final pretrial conference (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(f), (g)).
event FirstTrialSetting()
/// The producing party has actual notice that a document it produced will
/// be used (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-26(d)).
event ProducedDocumentUseNoticed()
/// A party's attorney serves interrogatory answers without the party's
/// signature (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-33(a)).
event UnexecutedAnswersServed()
/// Judgment is entered (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A proposed bill of costs is filed (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)).
event ProposedBillOfCostsFiled()
/// The clerk taxes costs (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)).
event CostsTaxed()
/// The case is finally disposed of, including any appeal (W.D. Tex. Local
/// Rule CV-79(a)).
event FinalDisposition()
/// The trial setting (W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-88(a)).
event TrialSetting()

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-3(a): a filing party who did not file a
/// complete and executed Civil Cover Sheet completes and executes it not
/// later than 7 days after the clerk informs it; otherwise the clerk
/// advises the court. Unrepresented and confined filers are exempt.
deadline cover-sheet-period: 7.days after CoverSheetDeficiencyNoticed() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-3(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(d)(2): a response to a discovery or case
/// management motion is filed not later than 7 days after the filing of
/// the motion; without a timely response the court may grant the motion
/// as unopposed.
deadline discovery-response-period: 7.days after DiscoveryMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(d)(2): a response to any other motion is
/// filed not later than 14 days after the filing of the motion, except as
/// Rule CV-15 provides.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)(2): a reply in support of a motion is filed
/// not later than 7 days after the filing of the response; absent leave,
/// no further submissions are allowed, and the court need not wait for the
/// reply.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-7(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-15(a): notwithstanding Rule CV-7's time limits,
/// a party may respond to a first FRCP 12(b) motion by filing an amended
/// pleading as a matter of course not later than 21 days after the filing
/// of the motion.
deadline amendment-as-of-course-period: 21.days after FirstRule12bMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-15(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(c): not later than 60 days after any
/// appearance of any defendant, the parties, having first conferred under
/// FRCP 26(f), submit a proposed scheduling order; the court sets the
/// dates in its discretion.
deadline proposed-scheduling-order-period: 60.days after DefendantAppeared() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(e): absent exceptional circumstances, no
/// motion relating to discovery is filed after the discovery deadline
/// unless it is filed within 14 days after the deadline and pertains to
/// conduct during the final 7 days of discovery.
deadline late-discovery-motion-period: 14.days after DiscoveryDeadline() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(f): unless the court orders otherwise, each
/// party serves and files its voir dire questions, stipulated facts,
/// exhibit and witness lists, deposition designations, proposed jury
/// instructions or findings, motions in limine and trial estimate at least
/// 14 days before the first of the scheduled dates for trial, jury
/// selection, docket call or the final pretrial conference.
deadline pretrial-disclosure-period: 14.days before FirstTrialSetting() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(g): at least 7 days before that date, each
/// party serves and files its objections to deposition designations and
/// exhibits and its responses to motions in limine; exhibit objections not
/// disclosed, other than under Federal Rules of Evidence 402 and 403, are
/// waived unless excused for good cause.
deadline pretrial-objection-period: 7.days before FirstTrialSetting() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-16(g)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-26(d)(2): once the producing party has actual
/// notice that a produced document will be used, it objects to the
/// document's authenticity within the time the court orders or Rule CV-16
/// specifies, and otherwise within 14 days; without a timely objection,
/// production authenticates the document for use against it.
deadline authenticity-objection-period: 14.days after ProducedDocumentUseNoticed() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-26(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-33(a): properly executed interrogatory answers
/// are served not later than 21 days after the attorney serves the
/// unexecuted answers; the court may extend the time.
deadline executed-answers-period: 21.days after UnexecutedAnswersServed() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-33(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)(1): a party awarded costs files and serves
/// a proposed bill of costs on Form AO 133 not later than 14 days after the
/// entry of judgment.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)(2): a party opposing the proposed bill of
/// costs notifies the requesting party not later than 7 days after it is
/// filed, and the parties confer.
deadline bill-of-costs-opposition-period: 7.days after ProposedBillOfCostsFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)(3): if a dispute remains, the joint or
/// requesting party's motion on the bill of costs is filed not later than
/// 21 days after the filing of the proposed bill.
deadline bill-of-costs-motion-period: 21.days after ProposedBillOfCostsFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)(5): a party dissatisfied with the clerk's
/// action may move for review not later than 7 days after the clerk has
/// taxed costs.
deadline cost-review-motion-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-54(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-79(a): the party offering an exhibit or
/// deposition removes it from the clerk's office within 60 days after the
/// final disposition of the case, including appeal; one remaining longer
/// may be destroyed or otherwise disposed of by the clerk.
deadline exhibit-removal: 60.days after FinalDisposition() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-79(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-88(a): unless specifically ordered otherwise,
/// the parties agree on an ADR method, provider, compensation and
/// completion date, and the ADR proceeding is completed not later than 60
/// days before the date of the trial setting.
deadline adr-completion-period: 60.days before TrialSetting() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D. Tex. Local Rule CV-88(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}
